id: pm-3dyec2
title: "All four graph traversal verbs reject the semantic edge kinds the ontology exists to express, so 'what implements this milestone' returns the ordering-kind answer with no sign a semantic one exists"
description: "Probed 2026-07-26: ancestors/descendants accept parent and child only; predecessors/successors accept blocks and blocked_by only; all four reject implements, verifies, related and discovered_from with 'Relationship kind implements is not a ordering kind'. The semantic kinds are traversable only via impact/dominators/centrality/communities/articulation; paths rejects --kind entirely; slack and redundancy reject semantic kinds. pm graph audit advertises implements and verifies in edges_by_kind, so the surface reports kinds its own traversal verbs refuse. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched graph traversal/kind/ontology items across all statuses; pm-ju83 (closed) built the relationship registry, pm-rggtvd covers hierarchy-kind cycle blindness, pm-6x7o covers edge validation and coverage, pm-4020c5 covers vocabulary fragmentation. No item covers the traversal verbs refusing the semantic kinds."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:graph","area:sdk",context-management,ontology,relationships
created_at: "2026-07-26T06:07:21.386Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T17:19:14.852Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The permitted kind set per traversal subcommand is derived from each kind's declared closure metadata rather than a hardcoded ordering-versus-hierarchy split, so a package registering a custom semantic kind gains traversal with no core change; default kind sets are unchanged so every existing invocation returns exactly what it returns today; a kind that genuinely cannot be traversed by a verb produces a redirect naming the subcommand that can traverse it instead of a bare 'is not a ordering kind'; pm graph paths accepts --kind or documents why it cannot; slack and redundancy carry a recorded disposition as supported or documented ordering-only rather than failing indistinguishably from an unsupported combination; docs and pm guide state which subcommand answers which question so impact --direction incoming being the provenance query is discoverable without reading source; a regression test asserts pm graph predecessors over implements returns the same node set as pm graph impact --direction incoming over implements"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Every declared relationship kind is traversable by the verb whose name matches the question it answers
value: Planning agents get the semantic answer from the verb they naturally reach for; the typed ontology becomes usable rather than merely stored; custom kinds registered by packages gain traversal without a core change
why_now: "The 2026-07-26 ladder pass raised implements to 286 and verifies to 91 edges connecting 268 of 271 active items to outcome milestones, so the semantic layer is now the most informative part of the graph and the traversal verbs are the only surface that cannot read it"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: low
confidence: high
